P3-RES-001 GREEN

Implementation commit: e666ab5c13521b98eec4720eb4dd5eb1a9fd81c0

Implemented a JDK-only DependencyGuard with fail-fast bulkhead, consecutive-
failure circuit opening, a 30-second open interval and one half-open probe. A
new backend-rpc-resilience Dubbo cluster-filter SPI applies one guard per
logical service call across Admin, App, Notification, Submission and Judge,
outside Dubbo's one safe query retry. Query/write/execution totals remain
800ms x2, 3s x1 and 190s x1; writes never gain automatic retries and business,
validation or authorization failures do not poison the circuit.

Direct HTTP boundaries are explicit: JWKS has an 800ms connect/read timeout
and a 300-second stale-key ceiling; OAuth has 5s/10s connect/read budgets and
provider-local guards; S3 has configurable 10s/30s connect/request budgets,
GET x2 and write x1 attempts plus a 16-call guard; MeiliSearch read, backfill,
worker and readiness paths use bounded guards while preserving explicit
database fallback semantics and Redis PEL recovery. Ban-check fallback now
fails closed when Auth cannot prove the account state.

Evidence:
- `bash scripts/test/dependency-resilience-contract.sh`: PASS; source/POM/YAML
  inventory and timeout/refusal/slow/open/half-open/recovery/saturation tests.
- Common/Dubbo/JWKS/OAuth/S3/Search/App focused tests: PASS.
- Affected 24-module reactor compile: BUILD SUCCESS.
- `bash scripts/dev/docs-contract-test.sh`: PASS.
- `bash scripts/dev/architecture-contract-test.sh`: PASS, including all prior
  owner, migration, backup, TLS, scheduler, lease and graceful-drain gates.
- YAML and shell syntax plus `git diff --check`: PASS.
- Graphify refreshed: 28,130 nodes, 83,911 edges, 887 communities.
- Codebase Memory coverage had no recorded gaps, but changed code was
  not-tracked/metadata-changed and scripts/docs were excluded in the older
